! CAM-B3LYP def2-SVP def2/J RIJCOSX TightSCF
# Gas-phase NEUTRAL (protonated) CR2 chromophore, charge 0, closed shell.
# Method-matched to the correlated ladder (same geometry, same def2-SVP basis)
# so TDDFT, EOM-CCSD, EOM-CCSD(fT) and STEOM are directly comparable. The
# neutral form is used because the isolated ANION has no bound electron-attached
# state in a diffuse basis, which breaks the EA-EOM sector of STEOM.
%maxcore 4000
%pal nprocs 8 end
%tddft
  NRoots 5
  TDA false
end
* xyzfile 0 1 neutral_chromophore.xyz
